# Where the Battlefield 6 catalog comes from

Everything here was read on **2026-10-10** (checked a second time that day
against EA's own pages). `catalog.json` is the single-kind form
(`kind: "weapons"`, Warzone's shape): Battlefield 6 is not built around
characters. Its four classes (Assault, Engineer, Support, Recon) each have a
signature weapon class under closed-weapon rules, but most playlists let any
class carry any gun, and the class shows only as a small icon in the squad
list, so the guns are the list.

**Pictures: none.** Every `image` is `null` (no official artwork fetched this
round). A picture added later must come from EA's own hosts.

## What is in Battlefield 6 today

- **Season 4**, in its third and last phase, **Tidal Strike** (since
  2026-09-15). The season's phases were Pacific Front (2026-07-21), Top Gun
  (2026-08-18) and Tidal Strike ([EA's Season 4 roadmap](https://www.ea.com/games/battlefield/battlefield-6/news/season-4-roadmap-everything-you-need-to-know),
  [EA's Tidal Strike guide](https://www.ea.com/games/battlefield/redsec/news/battlefield-season-4-update-event-guide)).
  `season` is written "Season 4: Tidal Strike" because that is the phase live
  today; EA titles the guide "Enter Tidal Strike: Battlefield Season 4 Update".
- **Season 5, "Siege of Vegas", starts 2026-10-13**, three days after this
  list, with four guns: **Mk 24** (assault rifle), **RSPR** (SMG), **Z84M**
  (LMG), **ELR-40** (bolt-action sniper rifle) ([EA's Season 5 roadmap](https://www.ea.com/games/battlefield/battlefield-6/news/battlefield-season-5-roadmap),
  dated 2026-10-09). They are **not** in the catalog yet, because they are not
  in the game; add them at the end of their groups once it is live.
- **80 items in 10 groups**: Assault Rifles 11, Carbines 9, SMGs 10, LMGs 10,
  DMRs 6, Sniper Rifles 6, Shotguns 4, Sidearms 7, Gadget weapons 11 (the
  launchers and the SS26, which replace the gun in the player's hands and the
