## Rarity (REDSEC only): `tiers`

REDSEC, the free battle royale, has six weapon rarities, named and coloured by
EA in [Battlefield REDSEC Battle Royale 101](https://www.ea.com/games/battlefield/redsec/news/battlefield-redsec-battle-royale-101),
lowest first: Common (white), Uncommon (green), Rare (blue), Advanced
(purple), Superior (orange), Unique (red). Checked again 2026-10-10. Weapon
Upgrade Kits raise a gun up to Advanced; Superior is "extremely rare; only a
few per match"; Unique are the player's own favourited Custom Weapons, from
Custom Weapon Drops. The `colour` values are the app's chips only, chosen from
EA's colour words, **not sampled from a frame** (D134: the Core learns each
tier's colour from the owner's crops). Where the colour shows on the REDSEC
HUD is not yet known.

## HUD states

*From public sources, not checked on a real frame.* What the screen shows in
each state, and what the Core could read there:

| State | What shows | What the Core could read |
|---|---|---|
| Deploy screen | Full-screen map, squad list, class and loadout picker | Not a play state: hold all Smart Actions. The loadout's gun names are printed here as text, the one place they surely are |
| On foot | Bottom right: the held gun's silhouette, magazine / reserve count, fire-mode icon. Bottom left: health (REDSEC: armour bar above it), backpack button | The gun's silhouette (picture teaching); the fire-mode icon; the ammo digits |
| Gadget held (launcher, SS26, M320A1) | The weapon panel switches to the gadget's icon and ammo | A gadget silhouette: the Gadget weapons group exists so a Smart Action can stand down |
| Scoped / ADS | Panel stays; a scope overlay fills the centre on high-zoom optics | Same panel |
| In a vehicle | The panel is replaced by the vehicle's HUD (seat, weapons, health) | "Not on foot": hold gun Smart Actions |
| Dead / spectating | Kill card, then the deploy screen | Hold everything |
| REDSEC | As on foot, plus the backpack, armour bar and ring timer; a gun's rarity colour (where on screen is unknown) | Rarity tier (D134) once its place is known |

**Does the HUD print the gun's name?** Probably not. An EA forum request
titled "Feature Request: Show weapon name on HUD (PS5 / console)"
([thread](https://forums.ea.com/discussions/battlefield-6-general-discussion-en/feature-request-show-weapon-name-on-hud-ps5--console/12899537),
read from search snippets only, HTTP 403) says only the weapon **icon and ammo
count** are shown. A [TechWiser icon guide](https://techwiser.com/battlefield-6-icons-symbols-meaning/)
describes the ammo readout as a weapon icon with numbers and a separate
fire-mode icon, and no name. A forum bug report places the weapon icon and
ammo bottom right. The first pass said the name "flashes for a moment on a
swap"; no source for that was found on recheck, so it is **unconfirmed**.

So Battlefield 6 is **not a name-reading game** on present evidence: the
route is **picture teaching** of the silhouette in the bottom-right panel. One
real frame of a weapon swap settles it; if a name does flash,
recognition.json's `"blank": "hold"` covers a name that fades.

## Update the list each season

Add each new gun at the end of its group with the season as `from` and the
season's roadmap or notes as `sources`; check EA's loadout page (it is updated
each season) for spellings; set `asOf` and `season`; run
`node dashboard/tools/test-game-data.js`.
